**F1 — high, blocker:** [validate_carry.go:91](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-501794006/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:91) checks the current worktree’s cleanliness but never establishes that the base validated its recorded commit.

A full validation can pass against an uncommitted fix while recording the original `git_head` and unavailable material provenance. Restore the original failing source, retain the canonical result, then run `--carry`: selection sees no source changes and carries the pass. The new run assigns current material provenance to that result. This breaks D1’s premise and can turn invalid evidence into current evidence.

Reject bases whose validated material cannot be established, and cover this sequence with a regression test. This finding follows from code inspection; the additional reproduction fixture was blocked by unavailable writable scratch space.

The existing carry and delivery-parser fixtures passed, and `go vet ./...` passed. Full validation did not complete. `artifact-check` reported a range ending at `6be3a6f…`, inconsistent with the requested `883eb1e…`; I stopped verification and cancelled the remaining checks. The draft below therefore **cannot satisfy the required-tool gate**.

Rules applied: pose-review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence. No attestation was recorded.

The assessment commands unexpectedly modified four derived files: `.pose/assessments/{integrations,technical-debt}.md` and `.pose/state/{integrations,technical-debt}.json`. Restoration was rejected by the read-only sandbox; those modifications remain. No implementation files were changed.

